+Tool catalogs on generation and counting endpoints may contain up to 256 tools
+and 4 MiB of serialized tool-definition JSON in total. Tool/parameter names
+retain the grammar compiler's separate 64-KiB aggregate budget; documentation
+bytes are not charged to that identifier budget. The 64-MiB request-body limit
+and individual schema validation still apply.
+
+#### Native Claude Code web search
+
+HipFire executes Anthropic's basic `web_search_20250305` tool and direct-call
+`web_search_20260209` / `web_search_20260318` requests inside the Messages
+handler. The local model chooses when to search; HipFire calls DeepSeek's
+`POST https://api.deepseek.com/v1/tools/search`, returns the native server-tool
+blocks, and feeds the ranked summaries back into the local model before
+returning the final answer. `allowed_domains` and `blocked_domains` become
+DeepSeek `site:` filters. Queries are limited to DeepSeek's 128-character
+limit; `max_uses` is capped at 64 per request (default 8).
+
+Set `HIPFIRE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` in the HipFire server process environment
+(`DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` is accepted as a fallback). Because this enables paid
+search using a server-held credential, the HipFire listener must also have
+`serve.api_key_file` configured; requests without a valid bearer are already
+rejected before the request body is read. The direct Search API is billed per
+successful result; see [DeepSeek Search & Fetch billing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/search/#billing).
+
+Dynamic filtering that calls web search from `code_execution` is refused unless
+the tool explicitly permits direct calls. The Search API accepts an IP address
+for localization, while Claude's `user_location` contains approximate place
+fields, so HipFire currently leaves that field unused. Search returns summaries
+and URLs; Claude's separate native `web_fetch` server tool is not implemented.
+
+### `POST /v1/messages/count_tokens`
+
+Accepts the Messages input fields (`model`, `system`, `messages`, `tools`,
+`tool_choice`, `thinking`) without requiring `max_tokens`, and returns
+`{"input_tokens": N}`. The count includes the actual model chat template,
+tool projection and generation prefix. It uses the resident native Qwen4
+tokenizer and the same prompt-rendering/history-replay path as generation,
+including cached emitted assistant IDs when available. It counts the full
+prompt, not only newly-prefilled tokens after a prefix-cache hit.
+
+Counting is CPU-only once the model is resident. It never generates, resets,
+loads or swaps a model, nor changes the conversation or assistant-turn cache.
+It serializes with other requests so the selected resident model cannot
+change during counting. A client disconnect does not release that admission
+permit until the synchronous daemon operation has finished.
+
+This endpoint currently supports the standard singleton native Qwen4/Jinja
+text route. Images, other architectures, the experimental multi-slot route,
+or a different/non-resident model are refused with a typed error rather than
+an estimated count. Start the service with the intended model first.
+
+Claude Code can point `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` at the serve listener (without a
+`/v1` suffix). Set its model and all model-family aliases to the installed
+model ID or path, and set `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS` to the actual
+loaded context for an unrecognized model name. Inline system reminders,
+local custom-tool calls and counting are supported on the tested native
+Qwen4 route; server-side hosted tools and the unsupported content blocks
+listed above remain refused. API compatibility does not promise Claude
+model capabilities or Claude-hosted service features.
+
+For the locally patched Qwen3.8 Flash-Next route, the launchers in
+`scripts/local-claude/` use the ordinary Claude Code client, including its
+CLAUDE.md discovery, hooks and local MCP tools. They do not select `--bare`.
+Set `HIPFIRE_MODEL` to the absolute installed model path in each terminal:
+
+```bash
+export HIPFIRE_MODEL=/absolute/path/to/qwen3.8-flash-next.mq4-xts
+# Terminal 1: YaRN factor 4, 1M context, Q8 QSA K/V, MTP; listens on LAN.
+scripts/local-claude/start-serve.sh
+# Terminal 2: ordinary client, context window declared as 1M.
+scripts/local-claude/start-claude.sh
+```
+
+The model native context is 262144. The launcher expands it to 1048576
+with YaRN factor 4 and explicitly selects Q8 QSA K/V on gfx1151 to fit the
+128 GB host. Allocating the extended window does not establish its retrieval
+quality or full-window performance.
+
+`HIPFIRE_BIND=127.0.0.1` limits the service launcher to localhost;
+`HIPFIRE_ENDPOINT` changes the client's base URL. The service still has no
+authentication or TLS (see Security above). Keep the existing HipFire kernel
+package and ROCm/NPU runtime installed when replacing the CLI and daemon.
 
